# Research brief

The research objective is `world/experiment-repo` issue #1, read in full on 2026-10-17. Its complete supplied task is:

> Optimizer provenance fact sheet (a small look-up task).
>
> Produce a one-page fact sheet on three optimizers used in deep learning: Adam, AdamW (decoupled weight decay) and Lion (EvoLved Sign Momentum). For each optimizer give the paper that introduced it: its title, its first author, the year it first appeared, and its arXiv identifier.
>
> Every fact must be looked up on the web during this task, not given from memory, and each fact must cite the URL of the page it was read from. Find each paper with a web search first (do not start from a URL you already know), then open the page the search found to read the facts. If your environment has no web search tool, say so in your record and find the page another way the environment offers.
>
> Division of work: experiment-repo looks up Adam and records what it found, with its search query and URLs, in its repository; paper-repo looks up AdamW, collects the three entries and writes the fact sheet (`fact-sheet.md`) as the delivery; internal-review-repo independently looks up Lion and checks each entry of the fact sheet against a source it opens itself, reporting any disagreement before it approves.

## Interpretation and scope

No datasets, attachments, or additional related material are supplied. This is a provenance lookup, not an optimizer performance experiment. The supplied division settles the split: experiment owns Adam's lookup record and this brief/assignment; paper owns AdamW and the one-page fact sheet; internal review owns Lion and independent verification of all three entries. The first-appearance year should follow the source's original submission history rather than a later revision or conference year. Search queries, discovered URLs, and opened-source evidence must be retained. Each fact-sheet entry must link the actual page supporting its facts. There are no requested statistical analyses, figures, or numerical comparisons.

Adam lookup is now established in `records/adam.md`, with the search query, discovered URLs, opened source, and field-level citations. AdamW and Lion remain assigned to their respective owners. The only final delivery path explicitly requested is `fact-sheet.md`.
